1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,150
Whether at school, college or work, most of us take some sort of lunch break.
无论是在学校、大学还是工作中，我们大多数人都会有某种形式的午休时间。

2
00:00:06,150 --> 00:00:15,240
It‘s a good time to have a rest, catch up with friends and eat some food - but here lies the dilemma - what to eat?
这是一个休息、和朋友聊聊天以及吃点东西的好时机——但这里存在一个两难境地——吃什么呢？

3
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:25,940
There are a feast of options but because of limited time or money, many of us stick to what we know - usually the humble sandwich.
选择可谓丰富多样，但由于有限的时间或金钱，我们很多人还是继续选择我们熟悉的食物——通常就是简单的三明治。

4
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:38,780
Some of us make our own sandwiches in the morning before heading out, whilst those in a rush tend to grab-and-go at a snack bar or a cafe or buy a meal deal at a supermarket.
我们中的一些人会在早上出门前自己制作三明治，而那些匆忙的人则倾向于在小吃店或咖啡馆买了就走，或者在超市购买套餐。

5
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:44,800
A packet of crisps may be an additional staple to our predictable lunch.
一包薯片可能是我们可以预见的午餐中额外的主食。

6
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:48,580
What we eat is usually the same everyday.
我们每天吃的东西通常都是一样的。

7
00:00:48,580 --> 00:00:59,180
Sheila Dillon from the BBC Food Programme says more than a third of office workers have eaten the same midday meal for the last nine months.
英国广播公司美食节目的希拉·狄龙说，在过去的九个月里，超过三分之一的上班族每天吃的午餐都是一样的。

8
00:00:59,180 --> 00:01:09,600
In the UK, bread has become the mainstay of our lunchtime snack, sometimes eaten at your desk - a style known as ’al-desko‘.
在英国，面包已经成为我们午间快餐的主要部分，有时人们会在办公桌前吃——这种方式被称为“在办公桌旁用餐”。

9
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:20,680
Bread is cheap and fills you up and with average lunch hours now reduced to 25 minutes, 24 seconds, it‘s quick and convenient to eat.
面包价格便宜，能让你吃饱，而且现在平均午餐时间缩短到了25分钟24秒，吃起来又快又方便。

10
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:23,530
But it's also boring!
但它也很无趣！

11
00:01:23,530 --> 00:01:35,040
Some people have broken the mould by bringing in leftovers from their previous night‘s dinner, which they then heat up in a microwave but even that isn't very exciting.
一些人打破了这种模式，把前一晚晚餐的剩菜带来，然后用微波炉加热，但即便如此也不是很令人兴奋。

12
00:01:35,040 --> 00:01:46,700
We are creatures of habit but philosopher Julian Baggini says “we‘re never going to break out of our midday malaise unless we think outside the box.”
我们是习惯的产物，但哲学家朱利安·巴吉尼说：“除非我们跳出常规思维，否则我们永远无法摆脱中午的这种不适状态。”

13
00:01:46,700 --> 00:01:50,590
There are alternatives that will fill you up.
还有其他能让你吃饱的选择。

14
00:01:50,590 --> 00:02:03,090
With just a microwave and a kettle, there are a number of hot satisfying meals than can be made such as soups and jacket potatoes served with a dollop of baked beans or cheese.
只要有一个微波炉和一个水壶，就可以做出许多令人满足的热食，比如汤和烤土豆，再配上一大块焗豆或奶酪。

15
00:02:03,090 --> 00:02:11,370
And then there are the ubiquitous instant noodles in a pot - although you may question how nutritious they are.
然后还有无处不在的即食泡面——尽管你可能会质疑它们的营养价值。

16
00:02:11,370 --> 00:02:20,540
If you‘ve got time for more exotic munchies, then look out for trendy ’Ottolenghi‘ style food such as fava bean salad wrap.
如果你有时间享用更异国风味的小吃，那就留意一下时尚的“奥托伦吉”风格的食物，比如蚕豆沙拉卷。

17
00:02:20,540 --> 00:02:30,950
There is also the healthy Japanese style ’bento box‘ or lunchbox that normally contains a mix of carbohydrate, protein and vegetable.
还有健康的日式“便当盒”，通常里面包含碳水化合物、蛋白质和蔬菜的混合搭配。

18
00:02:30,950 --> 00:02:34,880
And of course another healthy Japanese treat is sushi.
当然，另一种健康的日式美食就是寿司。

19
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:42,200
But if I’ve got time for a proper lunch, I head to my local greasy spoon and tuck into a fry-up.
但如果我有时间吃一顿像样的午餐，我会去当地的廉价小餐馆，尽情享用一顿油炸食物。

20
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:47,830
Not very healthy but delicious and it sets me up for an afternoon of hard work.
虽然不是很健康，但很美味，而且能让我为一下午的辛勤工作做好准备。

21
00:02:47,830 --> 00:02:52,340
Then it‘s time for the next dilemma - what to have for dinner?!
然后就到了下一个两难境地——晚餐吃什么呢？！

22
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:54,920
What do you usually eat for lunch?
你通常午餐吃什么呢？
